<Layout
	title="Privacy notice"
	description="How Oliver Hitchings collects, uses, stores and protects personal information."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-07-22')}
>
	<p>This notice explains how I use personal information when you visit this site, make an enquiry, become a client, or receive a relevant business introduction from me.</p>

	<h2>Who is responsible for your information</h2>
	<p>The data controller is <strong>Oliver Hitchings, sole trader</strong>. You can contact me about privacy or exercise your rights at <a href="mailto:hello@oliverhitchings.com">hello@oliverhitchings.com</a>.</p>

	<h2>Information I collect</h2>
	<p>Depending on how we interact, I may process:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>your name, work email address, role and business contact details;</li>
		<li>the company you work for and publicly available information about its services and online presence;</li>
		<li>information you submit through an enquiry form or send by email;</li>
		<li>project correspondence, requirements, approvals, contracts and payment records; and</li>
		<li>limited technical and security information produced when you use the site, such as IP address, browser details and request logs.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
	<p>Most information comes directly from you. For relevant business introductions, I may obtain professional contact information from <strong>public business sources</strong>, including a company website, Companies House, public business directories, maps listings and public professional profiles. I do not buy consumer mailing lists or guess email addresses.</p>

	<h2>Why I use it and my lawful bases</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Enquiries and requested steps:</strong> to answer you and take steps towards a contract.</li>
		<li><strong>Client work:</strong> to agree, deliver and administer services under our contract.</li>
		<li><strong>Relevant business introductions:</strong> to introduce website or automation services to appropriate corporate businesses. I rely on my <strong>legitimate interests</strong> in developing my business, balanced against the recipient’s rights and expectations, and apply the applicable electronic-marketing rules.</li>
		<li><strong>Site operation and security:</strong> to keep the site reliable, prevent abuse and understand faults, based on my legitimate interests.</li>
		<li><strong>Records and compliance:</strong> to meet tax, accounting and other legal obligations.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Direct marketing: your right to object</h2>
	<p><strong>You can object to direct marketing at any time.</strong> Reply “no thanks” to an outreach email or contact <a href="mailto:hello@oliverhitchings.com">hello@oliverhitchings.com</a>. I will stop marketing to you and retain only the minimum suppression record needed to respect your choice.</p>

	<h2>Who receives the information</h2>
	<p>I do not sell personal information. I share it only where necessary with service providers that help me run the business, such as Cloudflare for website hosting and security, Google for business email, and providers used to deliver an enquiry or an agreed client service. I may also disclose information to professional advisers, public authorities or law enforcement when legally required.</p>
	<p>These providers act under their own legal duties or contractual data-protection terms. Some may process information outside the UK. Where UK law requires a transfer mechanism, I rely on UK adequacy regulations or approved contractual safeguards.</p>

	<h2>How long I keep it</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Unsuccessful enquiries and prospective-business records: normally no more than <strong>12 months after the last meaningful contact</strong>.</li>
		<li>Client, contract, invoice and tax records: normally <strong>six years</strong> after the relevant engagement or accounting period.</li>
		<li>Security and operational logs: for the shortest practical period needed to operate and protect the service.</li>
		<li>Marketing suppression records: for as long as reasonably needed to ensure I continue to honour your objection.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>I may keep information longer where a legal claim, investigation or legal obligation requires it.</p>

	<h2>Your data-protection rights</h2>
	<p>Depending on the circumstances, you may ask for access to your information, correction, erasure, restriction, portability, or object to its use. If processing is based on consent, you can withdraw that consent. Contact me at <a href="mailto:hello@oliverhitchings.com">hello@oliverhitchings.com</a>. I may need to verify your identity before acting on a request.</p>

	<h2>No solely automated decisions</h2>
	<p>I do not make decisions about people that have legal or similarly significant effects using solely automated processing.</p>

	<h2>Cookies and site technology</h2>
	<p>I do not intentionally use advertising cookies or tracking pixels. The hosting and security infrastructure may use strictly necessary technology to deliver and protect the site. If non-essential cookies or analytics are introduced, this notice and the site’s consent controls will be updated first.</p>

	<h2>Security</h2>
	<p>I use proportionate technical and organisational measures to protect personal information, including access controls, local-first processing where practical, suppression controls and restricted credentials. No system is completely risk-free, but I review the controls used for sensitive workflows.</p>

	<h2>Questions and complaints</h2>
	<p>Please contact me first at <a href="mailto:hello@oliverhitchings.com">hello@oliverhitchings.com</a> so I can try to resolve your concern. You also have the right to complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/data-protection-complaints/" rel="noreferrer">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>, the UK data-protection regulator.</p>

	<h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
	<p>I review this notice when my services or use of personal information changes. The date above shows the latest revision.</p>
</Layout>
